; pset allocated a scratch vector for EVERY field write: list->vector
; walked the spine, vector-set! wrote the slot, vector->list consed a
; fresh 16-cell list back. A step writes ~13 fields, and most writes
; store the value the field already holds (a timer already at 0, a
; coyote already at max, a lane already on its target).
;
; This walks to slot i once, keeping the spine behind it. When the new
; value equals the old, the SAME player list comes back: no vector, no
; rebuild. When it differs, only the tail from slot i is consed; the
; cells in front are shared. Nothing mutates a player list (the values
; are a choice of the gate), so sharing the prefix is invisible.
;
; Same values, same order: the golden trace is unchanged.
(define (pset p i v)
  (let loop ((xs p) (n 0) (front (list)))
    (if (or (null? xs) (= n i))
      (if (and (pair? xs) (equal? (car xs) v))
        p
        (let rebuild ((ys front) (acc (cons v (if (pair? xs) (cdr xs) (list)))))
          (if (null? ys)
            acc
            (rebuild (cdr ys) (cons (car ys) acc)))))
      (loop (cdr xs) (+ n 1) (cons (car xs) front)))))
